From: HDSatelit <dev@hdsatelit.local>
Subject: [PATCH] JSC: allow the existing ARMv7 backends in an opt-in build

The 2.54 release archive still contains the ARMv7 assembler and 32/64
baseline and DFG implementations. PlatformEnable.h overrides the CMake
options on every JSVALUE32_64 build. Restrict that override to targets
other than Linux Thumb2 hard-float. FTL remains unavailable on ARM32.

Assert the effective options when the recipe explicitly requests them;
a successful build must not silently ship an interpreter as a JIT package.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [experimental product configuration]
---
diff --git a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformEnable.h b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformEnable.h
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformEnable.h
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformEnable.h
@@ -725,7 +725,7 @@
 #define ENABLE_JIT 1
 #endif
 
-#if USE(JSVALUE32_64)
+#if USE(JSVALUE32_64) && !(CPU(ARM_THUMB2) && CPU(ARM_HARDFP) && OS(LINUX))
 #undef ENABLE_JIT
 #define ENABLE_JIT 0
 #endif
@@ -757,9 +757,19 @@
 #if USE(JSVALUE32_64)
 #undef ENABLE_FTL_JIT
 #define ENABLE_FTL_JIT 0
+#if !(CPU(ARM_THUMB2) && CPU(ARM_HARDFP) && OS(LINUX))
 #undef ENABLE_DFG_JIT
 #define ENABLE_DFG_JIT 0
 #endif
+#endif
+
+#if defined(HDS_REQUIRE_JIT) && !ENABLE(JIT)
+#error "HDS requested JIT but the effective upstream configuration disables it"
+#endif
+
+#if defined(HDS_REQUIRE_DFG_JIT) && !ENABLE(DFG_JIT)
+#error "HDS requested DFG JIT but the effective upstream configuration disables it"
+#endif
 
 /* If possible, try to enable a disassembler. This is optional. We proceed in two
    steps: first we try to find some disassembler that we can use, and then we
